            "width": 1920
          }
        ],
        "name": "DogeDesigner",
        "text": "BREAKING: Ron Baron backs Elon Musk to put data centers in space.\n\n“We need more power and Elon’s doing that.”\n\n• Baron says America needs to build more chips at home and generate more electricity. “We need more power. Elon’s doing that.”\n\n• By Baron’s estimate, China has roughly 3× the power capacity of the U.S. and adds about 300 gigawatts a year, compared with 20 in the U.S.\n\n• Baron says Musk is targeting launches in 2027 and 2028 to bring solar-powered data centers into orbit.\n\n• He expects data centers in space to be “significant in 2028” and “huge” a year or two later.",
        "url": "https://x.com/cb_doge/status/2118715072155361739",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
      "retweet": null,
